{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1141 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "5cd7c1dbc2bf130898a419a73bee96f54f95afc8bf5e4f5d723bdd4b31b8a3e8" :edb/db-before-t 1140 :edb/db-after-t 1141 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534453 50 #inst "2026-10-07T05:12:05.043Z" 13194139534453 true] [17592186064012 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534453 false] [17592186064012 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534453 true] [17592186064012 1145 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x$. Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & \\Longrightarrow u^{\\prime } = 1 \\\\ v^{\\prime } = e^{7x} & \\Longrightarrow v = \\frac{1}{7}e^{7x}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int uv^{\\prime }dx &= uv - \\int vu^{\\prime }dx \\\\\n\\int x \\cdot e^{7x}dx &= x \\cdot \\frac{1}{7}e^{7x} - \\int\\frac{1}{7}e^{7x} \\cdot 1dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int xe^{7x}dx &= \\frac{1}{7}xe^{7x} - \\frac{1}{7}\\int e^{7x}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}xe^{7x} - \\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{e^{7x}}{7}) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}xe^{7x} - \\frac{1}{49}e^{7x} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534453 false] [17592186064012 1145 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534453 true] [17592186064013 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534453 false] [17592186064013 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534453 true] [17592186064013 1145 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x$. Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & \\Longrightarrow u^{\\prime } = 1 \\\\ v^{\\prime } = \\cos 2x & \\Longrightarrow v = \\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int uv^{\\prime }dx &= uv - \\int vu^{\\prime }dx \\\\\n\\int x\\cos 2xdx &= x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2x - \\int\\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2x \\cdot 1dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int x\\cos 2xdx &= \\frac{1}{2}x\\sin 2x - \\frac{1}{2}\\int\\sin 2xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}x\\sin 2x - \\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos 2x) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}x\\sin 2x + \\frac{1}{4}\\cos 2x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534453 false] [17592186064013 1145 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534453 true] [17592186064030 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534453 false] [17592186064030 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534453 true] [17592186064030 1145 "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534453 true] [17592186064030 1145 "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & \\Longrightarrow u^{\\prime } = 1 \\\\ v^{\\prime } = \\sin (5x) & \\Longrightarrow v =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cos (5x)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int uv^{\\prime }dx &= uv - \\int vu^{\\prime }dx \\\\\n\\int x \\cdot \\sin (5x)dx &= -x \\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\cos (5x) - \\int(-\\frac{1}{5}\\cos (5x)) \\cdot 1dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\sin (5x)dx &= \\left.- \\frac{1}{5}x\\cos (5x)\\right|_{0}^{\\pi /5} + \\frac{1}{5}\\int_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\cos (5x)dx \\\\\n&= \\left.- \\frac{1}{5}x\\cos (5x)\\right|_{0}^{\\pi /5} + \\left.\\frac{1}{5}((\\sin (5x))/(5))\\right|_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\\n&= [- \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\cos (\\pi ) + \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos (0)] + [\\frac{1}{25}\\sin (\\pi ) - \\frac{1}{25}\\sin (0)] \\\\\n&= [- \\frac{\\pi }{25} \\cdot (-1) + 0] + [0 - 0] \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\pi }{25}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534453 false] [17592186064157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289105 13194139534453 true] [17592186064157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289112 13194139534453 true] [17592186064157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289119 13194139534453 true] [17592186064157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289154 13194139534453 true] [17592186064157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289168 13194139534453 true] [17592186064158 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289126 13194139534453 true] [17